Day 3 of 90 with @MyFirstHack, and today I did something I never thought I'd do: I ran a security audit on myself.
I went in expecting it to feel technical and complicated. Instead it felt like finally looking at the locks on my own front door.
I found 5 gaps across my accounts. The biggest one? My email had shown up in 3 data breaches without me knowing. I fixed what I could right away by turning on authenticator-app 2FA for my primary email.
What stuck with me: your email isn't just an account. It's the master key to every account linked to it.
Portfolio piece number one is done. 87 days to go. 🔐
